<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Châtillon</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Châtillon was a French noble family from Châtillon-sur-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marne">Marne</a> in Champagne, prominent from the 11th to the 15th century. Its members held the counties of Blois, Saint-Pol and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/penthievre">Penthièvre</a> and included Gaucher V de Châtillon, constable of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-of-blois">Charles of Blois</a>, claimant to the duchy of Brittany. The family ruled Blois from the 1230s until Guy II sold it in 1391.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-chatillon.jpg" alt="House of Châtillon" width="320" height="374" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: MostEpic · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arms_of_the_house_of_Ch%C3%A2tillon.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>From the 1230s the house of <b>Châtillon</b> held Blois.</blockquote><a href="/state/county-of-blois">County of Blois</a></li></ul></section>
